## Objective

Close the Tameion hackathon prototype into a truthful, judge-ready product by **11 Oct 2026** without reopening broad AP/ERP scope.

Core invariant remains: **NO ASSURANCE, NO EXECUTION**. AI may assess/propose only. Human authorization and deterministic assurance remain mandatory. No mainnet.

## 365 audit snapshot — 2 Oct 2026

### Completed / verified product milestones

- **J0 bootstrap/connectivity/genuine usage closure:** #1 / #40 closed.
- **ERP/source → Tameion control → Circle/Arc settlement boundary:** #20 decision implemented by #21.
- **Finance Agent grounding:** #17 closed.
- **Live NVIDIA capability:** #45 closed; protected synthetic provider proof PASS.
- **J1 genuine-obligation assessment:** #41 closed truthfully at **J1_NO_CANDIDATE / STOP**. No genuine PAY candidate was forced.
- **Dual-path demo:** #44 closed; isolated SIMULATED_HAPPY_PATH uses FAKE_TESTNET_ADAPTER and is explicitly non-economic.
- **Judge/demo evidence pack:** #42 closed.
- **Assessment operator UI:** #46 / PR #49 merged and AXIS_PASS.
- **Durable assessment core:** current carrier contains append-only assessment history, exact assessment identity/hash authorization binding and Supabase-backed snapshot persistence; focused durability/history tests are green. #18 remains open for residual/full acceptance rather than because the core mechanism is absent.

### Current execution lane

**#15-A — HOLD/ESCALATE Attention Required report**

Admitted scope remains only the truthful read-only HOLD/ESCALATE projection. Paid/Reconciled and Execution Register remain deferred until authoritative settled/execution data exists.

Current preserved branch/worktree: reports-hold-15a at base 9633540d6fbd9e6e52a3902aee152d8da1390450.

## Submission-critical roadmap

### Gate 1 — Recover and close #15-A
1. Resume the existing preserved three-file worktree; no competing writer.
2. Verify focused report tests + already-established critical regressions.
3. One commit/non-force push, PR, one FORGE_TERMINAL_RECEIPT v1.
4. AXIS lightweight functional review.
5. Merge/close if PASS.

### Gate 2 — Visual integration / judge-facing polish
Re-enter #14 **now as a presentation-layer milestone** after #15-A. The previous requirement to wait for all of #12/#13/#16 and an authentic product payment is superseded for hackathon closeout because the genuine J1 lane correctly has no PAY candidate.

Use the existing Stitch/Figma references as **REFERENCE_ONLY**:
- preserve five-screen information architecture;
- port approved color/type/spacing/component patterns;
- improve navigation, tables, hierarchy, state clarity and evidence presentation;
- use only real current state or explicitly labelled synthetic demo state;
- do not copy fictional users/vendors/hashes/confidence scores/HSM claims or generated control semantics;
- no payment, authorization, PAE, Safety Kernel, provider, persistence or idempotency behavior changes.

### Gate 3 — Exact deployed demo QA
Verify one exact candidate deployment end-to-end:
- Obligations → Assessment → Authorization → Assurance & Execution → Reconciliation/Evidence;
- genuine lane visibly terminates fail-closed at J1_NO_CANDIDATE / STOP;
- synthetic happy path is unmistakably labelled simulated/non-economic;
- HOLD/ESCALATE report works;
- no misleading green PAY authority;
- UNKNOWN/no-blind-retry/idempotency boundaries remain truthful;
- no secrets/private financial destinations exposed;
- desktop browser QA and one compact responsive pass.

### Gate 4 — Product-truth/docs consolidation
- Replace stale README/status statements with current verified truth.
- PR #43 is historical/stale and must not merge as-is.
- Bring README, demo runbook and submission narrative into agreement with the exact final deployment/head.
- Keep authentic Arc product transfer described accurately: it is not required to invent a genuine payable candidate. Any future real testnet payment still requires a valid exact intent plus fresh Prime authorization.

### Gate 5 — Submission freeze
- freeze exact final head;
- smallest relevant regression suite + typecheck/build/hygiene;
- verify Vercel READY exact SHA;
- verify demo evidence/runbook against deployed behavior;
- no new feature work after freeze except material defect correction.

## Deferred / post-hackathon backlog

Unless a final QA defect requires a bounded correction, defer:
- #11 broad Agent Runtime hardening;
- #12 multi-invoice allocation engine;
- #13 Evidence Vault/PDF/XML ingress;
- #16 broader PaymentIntent/reservation/recovery domain expansion;
- #19 arc-agent-kit research;
- residual/full #18 UX/history expansion;
- #15 Paid & Reconciled and Execution Register until authoritative backing truth exists;
- ERP-specific connectors and general FX/GL/treasury scope.

## Completion definition

Tameion is submission-ready when:
1. #15-A is closed or deliberately removed from final scope with no broken UI;
2. five-screen UI is visually coherent and truth-bound;
3. genuine fail-closed path and synthetic happy path are both demonstrable;
4. exact deployed path passes browser QA;
5. public README/demo docs match current truth;
6. exact final head is frozen with green focused/critical checks;
7. no retained payment/provider mutation is performed without the required explicit human gate.

